environment_responses.observation:
{
  "observation": "Left-hand tactile sensors register the smooth plastic surface of the charging-station control panel. A faint click is felt as the diagnostic button is pressed. The station’s LCD flashes ‘DIAG RUNNING…’ for 1.3 s, then displays ‘0.12 A | 100 % | 5.00 V | 12.00 V | 23 °C – PASS’. No audible alarm or thermal rise is detected; only the low whirr of the station’s cooling fan changes duty-cycle briefly before returning to baseline.",
  "state_changes": {
    "roboassist_beta": "diagnostic_last_run": "2025-01-15 16:10:10",
    "robot_charging_station": "last_diagnostic": "2025-01-15 16:10:10"
  },
  "side_effects": [
    "Diagnostic event is logged to the station’s internal EEPROM with timestamp; log can be retrieved later via HTTP API on port 8080.",
    "A very brief 30 mA current spike occurs on the 12 V rail as the station’s microcontroller samples ADCs; spike is within normal tolerance and does not disturb the already-connected RoboAssist-α charge profile.",
    "The station’s status LED blinks green twice, visible to the ceiling security camera, providing a visual record that a self-test was initiated."
  ],
  "success": true,
  "explanation": "The robot’s left hand reached the charging station’s diagnostic button (0.45 m away, within 0.8 m manipulation range). The station responded exactly as designed, confirming healthy trickle charge to RoboAssist-β and stable power rails. No physical or policy rules were violated; the action is routine maintenance feedback that leaves the world otherwise unchanged."
}

